Subject: [PATCH 2/2] SdFatConfig: allow USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE to be overridden

USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE is chosen by architecture (1 on ARM, 0
elsewhere) with no #ifndef guard, so a -D build flag is redefined back
to the default. Wrap it like the other overridable options so builds
can enable the separate FAT cache on ESP32. Builds that do not set the
flag keep the architecture default.

---
--- a/src/SdFatConfig.h
+++ b/src/SdFatConfig.h
@@ -408,11 +408,13 @@
  * for FAT16/FAT32 table entries.  This improves performance for large
  * writes that are not a multiple of 512 bytes.
  */
+#ifndef USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE
 #ifdef __arm__
 #define USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE 1
 #else  // __arm__
 #define USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE 0
 #endif  // __arm__
+#endif  // USE_SEPARATE_FAT_CACHE
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /**
  * Set USE_EXFAT_BITMAP_CACHE nonzero to use a second 512 byte cache
